  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Total obligations for Computer Systems Design Services (NAICS 541512) in FY2026 to date are $19.7B. Obligations fell 37.9% year over year. There have been 8,866 awards so far, with an average award size of $2.2M. By fiscal year, obligations were $26.7B in FY21, $29.9B in FY22, $30.5B in FY23, $33.4B in FY24, and $31.7B in FY25. Buying in FY2026 to date is led by the General Services Administration at $4.1B, the Department of Defense at $3.9B, and the Department of Veterans Affairs at $3.1B. Other top buyers include the Department of Health and Human Services at $2.4B and the Department of Homeland Security at $1.7B. The largest vendors in FY2026 to date are ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC at $1.8B, GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. at $1.5B, and ORACLE HEALTH GOVERNMENT SERVICES, INC. at $1.3B. BOOZ ALLEN HAMILTON INC has $1.1B, and several other named vendors have obligations between $521M and $857M. The current-year totals are partial and reflect fiscal year to date activity.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why did obligations fall in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "Obligations in FY2026 to date are $19.7B, down 37.9% year over year. That drop follows several larger recent years, including $33.4B in FY24 and $31.7B in FY25. The FY2026 total is partial, recorded across 8,866 awards with an average award size of $2.2M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate the market now?",
        "body": "The General Services Administration leads buying at $4.1B, followed by the Department of Defense at $3.9B and the Department of Veterans Affairs at $3.1B. Top vendors are ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC at $1.8B, GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. at $1.5B, and ORACLE HEALTH GOVERNMENT SERVICES, INC. at $1.3B. Other named vendors include BOOZ ALLEN HAMILTON INC at $1.1B, DELOITTE CONSULTING LLP at $857M, and ANDURIL INDUSTRIES, INC. at $521M."
      }
    ]
  },
